ack ack ack... after playing nethack (vanilla) for 3 years, I've never
even entered the fake wizards tower.

Now suddenly I have a possible ascension run with a chaotic elf
wizard. Armed with the Finger of Death spell, I kick Rodney's butt
each time he showed his ugly face. Air elementals was easier than I
thought with my FoD spell and 2x wand of Death. The ring of Conflict
was a huge help in the elemental planes too, oh yeah also having an AC
-40 was probably a huge help...

Unfortunately, wearing the ring of Conflict into the Astral Plane
generated 4 hostile angels around me! No worries, wearing the Eye of
Aethiopeca, Magicbane and the full host of intrinsic, clearing out the
surrounding area wasn't even difficult. Not even with Death and Famine
trying to crash my party.

Ring of Conflict also meant that this guy (looks like a archeologist)
Richard the adventurer helped clear my periphery with his
Snickersnee's insta-death decapitation .

Dang! I was cornered by Famine, and an Archon when trying to reach an
altar - so the only clear way was towards the Snickersnee wielding
archologist -> the following happened:
- Richard hits you!
- You are decapitated by Snickersnee!
- You are dead, dead, dead...

Crap! The guy manages a decapitation on his first hit? My AC was
-40!!!

So, my question is: Should I have cast Finger of Death on him as soon
as I got a clear shot? I was trying to keep him in my periphery to
clear out any new spawned monster while I was heading for the altars.
I was wanted to conserve my spellpoints to cast FoD against the riders
and priests (except Death of course).


